{"name":"Squash","hex":"#f2ab15","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Squash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Squash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Squash (sport)","blocks":[{"text":"Squash, sometimes called squash rackets, is a racket sport played by two (singles) or four players (doubles) in a four-walled court with a small, hollow, rubber ball. The players alternate striking the ball with their rackets, directing it onto the playable surfaces of the four walls of the court. The object of the game is to hit the ball in such a way that the opponent is unable to play a valid return. There are about 20 million people who play squash regularly worldwide in over 185 countries. The governing body of squash, World Squash, is recognized by the International Olympic Committee, and the sport will be included in the Olympic Games, starting in the 2028 Summer Olympics in Los Angeles. The Professional Squash Association (PSA) organizes the pro tour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Semifinal_Squash_SM_2021.jpg/330px-Semifinal_Squash_SM_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squash_(sport)","wikidata":"Q133201"},{"title":"Cucurbita","blocks":[{"text":"Cucurbita is a genus, native to the Andes and Mesoamerica, of herbaceous fruits in the gourd family, Cucurbitaceae. Five edible species are grown and consumed for their flesh and seeds. They are variously known as squash, pumpkin, or gourd, depending on species, variety, and local parlance. Other kinds of gourd, also called bottle gourds, are native to Africa and belong to the genus Lagenaria, which is in the same family and subfamily as Cucurbita, but in a different tribe; their young fruits are eaten much like those of the Cucurbita species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Squashes_at_Kew_Gardens_IncrEdibles_2013.jpg/330px-Squashes_at_Kew_Gardens_IncrEdibles_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucurbita","wikidata":"Q5339301"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Squash_Played_at_the_Pyramids_of_Egypt.jpg/500px-Squash_Played_at_the_Pyramids_of_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Squash_Played_at_the_Pyramids_of_Egypt.jpg/500px-Squash_Played_at_the_Pyramids_of_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Squash played at the Great Pyramids of Egypt","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASquash_Played_at_the_Pyramids_of_Egypt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Nanoldsquash2.JPG/500px-Nanoldsquash2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Nanoldsquash2.JPG/1280px-Nanoldsquash2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Nanoldsquash2.JPG/500px-Nanoldsquash2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old and new style squash rackets","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANanoldsquash2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Squash_Ball_Dunlop_Revelation_Pro_1.jpg/500px-Squash_Ball_Dunlop_Revelation_Pro_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Squash_Ball_Dunlop_Revelation_Pro_1.jpg/1280px-Squash_Ball_Dunlop_Revelation_Pro_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Squash_Ball_Dun